1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,688
First of all I'd just like to say,

2
00:00:02,688 --> 00:00:07,728
Cristina and Ibrahim, that I really enjoyed watching your video about student life last week,

3
00:00:07,728 --> 00:00:11,760
and I could see that the rest of the group did too.

4
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:15,660
You did really well, and I hope that you got a lot out of it.

5
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:19,680
I'd like to use this tutorial as a feedback session

6
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,640
where you reflect on the experience of doing the project.

7
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:29,590
So Cristina, I was wondering, what did you enjoy most about making the video?

8
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:32,310
I liked using the camera.

9
00:00:32,310 --> 00:00:35,000
Is it the first time you've operated one like that?

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,190
Yes, it is.

11
00:00:36,190 --> 00:00:39,100
Well the results were very good! Anything else?

12
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:43,720
I also enjoyed visiting one of the British students we filmed

13
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:46,620
I'd never been inside a British home before.

14
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:51,080
OK Cristina, thanks. What about you, Ibrahim? What did you enjoy?

15
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:55,060
Well for me it was a very good chance to get to know students

16
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:56,140
who are on other courses,

17
00:00:56,140 --> 00:00:58,271
because everyone in our group is studying English,

18
00:00:58,271 --> 00:01:02,000
and we don't usually have much to do with the rest of the college.

19
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,950
Yes, good. Do you think you'll maintain the contact now?

20
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:09,590
I hope so. I've invited three of them to have dinner with me next week.

21
00:01:09,590 --> 00:01:12,280
Great! If you haven't decided what to make

22
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:15,583
yet I can tell you they'll love trying Arab dishes.

23
00:01:15,583 --> 00:01:18,580
And of course, it's good for your English too.

24
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:20,156
Cristina, what did you find?

25
00:01:20,156 --> 00:01:25,830
What was the most useful aspect of the project from the point of view of the English practice?

26
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:30,460
I think, when we were being shown how to edit the film

27
00:01:30,740 --> 00:01:32,220
we had to follow the instructions.

28
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:35,060
And that was very good practice for me.

29
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:39,320
And I also learned some technical words that I hadn't heard before.

30
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:43,620
What about you Ibrahim? What was the most useful for your English?

31
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:45,664
It was listening to the British students,

32
00:01:45,664 --> 00:01:49,753
because they don't speak as slowly as most of the tutors on our course.

33
00:01:49,753 --> 00:01:54,426
I think they speak at natural speed, so it forces me to get used to it.

34
00:01:54,426 --> 00:01:56,470
And they use a lot of slang.

35
00:01:56,470 --> 00:01:59,300
So you learned some new words which will be useful?

36
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:00,070
Yes.

37
00:02:00,070 --> 00:02:02,079
Good. I'm glad it helped.

38
00:02:02,079 --> 00:02:08,060
Well, we've talked a little bit about enjoyment, and about language practice

39
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:08,911
Were there any other benefits?

40
00:02:08,911 --> 00:02:15,340
What else did you feel you'd learnt from the project? Was it useful in other ways?

41
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:19,638
Yes, well firstly, I learned how to use a video camera.

42
00:02:19,638 --> 00:02:25,500
And also, I think I really learned a lot about working together with other people.

43
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:28,560
I've never done anything with a group before

44
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:33,268
and we had to find ways of cooperating,

45
00:02:33,268 --> 00:02:37,020
erm, and compromising, and sometimes persuading people

46
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:39,580
when they don't agree with you.

47
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:42,850
Yes, that is a very useful experience, I know.

48
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:44,750
What about you, Ibrahim?

49
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:48,169
Well, I think I learnt a lot about how important editing is.

50
00:02:48,169 --> 00:02:51,302
When you're filming you think that everything's going to be interesting,

51
00:02:51,302 --> 00:02:56,430
but in fact we cut around half of it in the end, and then it was much better.

52
00:02:56,430 --> 00:03:00,520
Good. Well, one last thing I'd like to ask

53
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:03,907
What mistakes do you think you, as a group that is, made?

54
00:03:03,907 --> 00:03:07,700
I mean, to put it another way

55
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:11,740
if you had to do it all over again, is there anything you'd do differently?

56
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:13,624
We didn't plan very well.

57
00:03:13,624 --> 00:03:17,200
For example, we didn't decide on dates

58
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,654
when we'd complete each separate step of the project,

59
00:03:19,654 --> 00:03:23,200
and we should have agreed about that in the beginning

60
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:26,060
because we were always late with everything!

61
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:27,810
Right. Anything else?

62
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:32,235
I think we should have tried to experiment more with the camera.

63
00:03:32,235 --> 00:03:36,660
I mean with angles, and the focus and that kind of thing.

64
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:39,960
So you should have been more ambitious? Do you agree, Ibrahim?

65
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:43,137
Not really. In fact, I think we were too ambitious.

66
00:03:43,137 --> 00:03:47,500
We were inexperienced, and we didn't have a lot of time

67
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:50,444
and we tried to do too much, to make a long film.

68
00:03:50,444 --> 00:03:55,210
Next time I would make a shorter one and try to get the quality better.

69
00:03:55,210 --> 00:04:01,844
Well, that's very interesting. Next semester we will be doing another video project-with a different content,

70
00:04:01,844 --> 00:04:08,062
of course, but you'll have an opportunity to put into practice what you've learnt this time.

71
00:04:08,062 --> 00:04:10,550
Do you have any ideas about...
